Reference: https://github.com/illusioneering/textured-mesh-simplification
Snapshot: 3b9195c (2026)
Author: Evan Suma Rosenberg
License: MIT (LICENSE.txt)

The native experimental Wild QEM geometry backend is adapted from the area-weighted plane
quadrics, dynamic boundary-area quadrics, and vertex-pair collapse ideas in this reference.
Its implementation is in source/blender/geometry/intern/decimate_wild.cc.

The reference is an independent implementation of Liu, Zhang and Yuksel,
"Simplifying Textured Triangle Meshes in the Wild", SIGGRAPH Asia 2025.
This backend is not the authors' official implementation and does not implement texture-atlas
rebaking or the paper's complete correspondence pipeline. It resamples Blender attributes.
